                <pb facs="0362" n="258" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg258"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.00/3058: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Germany (Dodd)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-08-20T19:00:00-04:00">August 20, 1933—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. In spite of the presentation made in your 131, August 20, 2 p.m., I continue
                    to feel that this Government should not take the lead in this matter. The
                    British and French have as much if not more at stake than we, and I should not
                    wish to give them an opportunity later to justify a decision by claiming that it
                    was made at the instance of this gov’t, or in pursuance of its advice. In
                    leaving the matter to your discretion, we are of course prepared to support you
                    in any decision you may make.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
